## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
as-path-limit <limit>
as-path-limit
undo as-path-limit
FuncDef:
The as-path-limit command sets the maximum number of AS numbers in the AS_Path attribute.
The undo as-path-limit command restores the default setting.
By default, no limit is configured on the maximum number of AS numbers in the AS_Path attribute, but the maximum number of AS numbers carried in the AS_Path attribute is limited by the BGP message length.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'limit', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum number of AS numbers in the AS_Path attribute.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 2000. The default value is 255.\nThe maximum value of limit for the 2-byte and 4-byte AS number is the same.\nIf limit is not specified, the maximum number of AS numbers in the AS_Path attribute is 255.'}
