## User question:
How to configure Huawei router's BGP to immediately reset EBGP sessions when the local interface goes down in a VPN instance IPv4 address family?
---
## Proposed answer:
interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1
undo shutdown
exit
bgp 100
peer 2.2.2.2 connect-interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1
vpn-instance vpna
ipv4-family unicast
undo synchronization
undo peer 2.2.2.2 enable
peer 2.2.2.2 reset-timer hold-time
quit
quit
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
ebgp-interface-sensitive
undo ebgp-interface-sensitive
FuncDef:
The ebgp-interface-sensitive command immediately resets BGP sessions between the local interface and directly connected EBGP peers if the local interface goes Down.
The undo ebgp-interface-sensitive command disables the function.
By default, this function is enabled.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
