## User question:
How to configure a Huawei router to remove all private AS numbers from the AS_Path attribute when advertising BGP updates to peer group "CUSTOMER_EDGE", while preserving their AS path length by replacing them with the local AS number?
---
## Proposed answer:
peer-group CUSTOMER_EDGE
undo inherit-as-path
as-path-filter remove-private-sequence out
quit
ip as-path access-list remove-private-sequence
permit ^4[0-9]{2}|[5-9][0-9]{2}|[1-2][0-9]{3}|3[0-2][0-9]{2}|33[0-4][0-9]|335[0-4]$
