## User question:
Configure a Huawei router to establish a BGP peering with neighbor 192.168.5.8 using fake AS 65050 while prepending both the fake and global AS numbers in outbound updates.
---
## Proposed answer:
peer 192.168.5.8 as-number 65050
peer 192.168.5.8 connect-interface LoopBack0
peer 192.168.5.8 next-hop-local
peer 192.168.5.8 advertise-community
peer 192.168.5.8 as-override
peer 192.168.5.8 route-policy PREPEND out
route-policy PREPEND permit node 10
if-match acl 3000
apply community 65000:65050
route-policy PREPEND permit node 20
if-match acl 3001
apply as-path prepend 65000 65050
---
