## User question:
How to configure BGP whitelist session CAR parameters on a Huawei router with CIR 48 kbit/s, CBS 30000 bytes, PIR 50000 kbit/s, and PBS 6500000 bytes?
---
## Proposed answer:
car inbound cir 48000 cbs 30000 pir 50000000 pbs 6500000
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
whitelist session-car bgp { cir <cir-value> | cbs <cbs-value> | pir <pir-value> | pbs <pbs-value> } *
undo whitelist session-car bgp [ { cir <cir-value> | cbs <cbs-value> | pir <pir-value> | pbs <pbs-value> } * ]
FuncDef:
The whitelist session-car bgp command sets values for the BGP whitelist session CAR parameters.
The undo whitelist session-car bgp command restores the default values for the BGP whitelist session CAR parameters.
By default, the CIR, CBS, PIR, and PBS of BGP whitelist session CAR are 24 kbit/s, 15000 bytes, 48000 kbit/s, and 6000000 bytes, respectively.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'cir cir-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a committed information rate (CIR), that is, the average rate at which packets can be transmitted or forwarded.\nThe value ranges from 24 to 1200, in kbit/s. The default value is 24.'}
{'Parameters': 'cbs cbs-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a committed burst size (CBS), which limits the maximum number of bytes available for a burst of packets in a short interval to remain within CIR.\nThe value ranges from 15000 to 1500000, in bytes. The default value is 15000.'}
{'Parameters': 'pir pir-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a peak information rate (PIR), that is, the peak rate at which packets can be transmitted or forwarded.\nThe value ranges from 12000 to 60000, in kbit/s. The default value is 48000.'}
{'Parameters': 'pbs pbs-value', 'Info': 'Specifies a peak burst size (PBS), which limits the maximum number of bytes available for a burst of packets in a short interval to remain within PIR.\nThe value ranges from 1500000 to 7500000, in bytes. The default value is 6000000.'}
