## User question:
How to enable BGP multi-instance with AS number 65001 and instance name "INTERNET" on a Huawei router?
---
## Proposed answer:
ip vpn-instance INTERNET
ipv4-family
route-distinguisher 65001:1
quit
bgp 65001 instance INTERNET
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
bgp <as-number> instance <instance-name>
undo bgp <as-number> instance <instance-name>
FuncDef:
The bgp instance command enables BGP and enter the BGP multi-instance view.
The undo bgp instance command disables BGP.
By default, the BGP is disabled.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'as-number', 'Info': 'Specifies a destination AS number.\nFor an integral AS number, the value is an integer ranging from 1 to 4294967295.\nFor an AS number in dotted notation, the value is in the format of x.y, where x and y are integers ranging from 1 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively.'}
{'Parameters': 'instance instance-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a BGP multi-instance.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 31 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
