## User question:
"How to enable modification of VPN-Target and SoO extended community attributes in matched BGP routes using route-policies on a Huawei router?"
---
## Proposed answer:
ip community-list standard VPN-Target
route-policy VPN-Target permit node 10
if-match ip community-list 1
set extcommunity cost 100
set extcommunity rt 1:1
set extcommunity soo 2:2
ip community-list standard SoO
route-policy SoO permit node 10
if-match ip community-list 2
set extcommunity soo 3:3
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
ext-community-change enable
undo ext-community-change enable
FuncDef:
The ext-community-change enable command enables a device to use route-policies to change the VPN-Target and SoO extended community attributes in matched BGP routes.
The undo ext-community-change enable command disables a device from using route-policies to change the VPN-Target or SoO extended community attribute in matched BGP routes.
By default, a BGP device cannot use route-policies to change the VPN-Target or SoO extended community attribute in matched BGP routes.
