## User question:
How to configure Huawei router's BGP multi-instance to allow peer 192.168.50.25 up to 200 seconds for reestablishing BGP session during graceful restart?
---
## Proposed answer:
bgp 100 instance p1
peer 192.168.50.25 graceful-restart timer restart 200
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> graceful-restart timer restart <time-value>
undo peer <ipv4-address> graceful-restart timer restart
FuncDef:
The peer graceful-restart timer restart command sets the maximum duration on a device for a specified peer to wait for its BGP peer relationship to be reestablished with the device. After the command is run, the device will advertise the maximum duration to the specified peer.
The undo peer graceful-restart timer restart command deletes the configured duration.
By default, a peer specified on a device waits for its BGP peer relationship to be reestablished for a maximum of 150 seconds.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a BGP peer.\nThe value is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'time-value', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum duration on a device for a peer to wait for its BGP peer relationship to be reestablished with the device.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 3 to 3600, in seconds.'}
