## User question:
Configure BFD detection parameters on a Huawei router for peer 172.16.32.45 with transmit interval 150ms, receive interval 120ms, and detection multiplier 8.
---
## Proposed answer:
peer 172.16.32.45 bfd min-tx-interval 150 min-rx-interval 120 detect-multiplier 8
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> bfd { min-tx-interval <min-tx-interval> | min-rx-interval <min-rx-interval> | detect-multiplier <multiplier> } *
undo peer <ipv4-address> bfd { min-tx-interval <min-tx-interval> | min-rx-interval <min-rx-interval> | detect-multiplier <multiplier> } *
FuncDef:
The peer bfd command sets BFD detection parameters for a peer.
The undo peer bfd command restores default BFD detection parameter values.
By default, the interval at which BFD packets are sent is 10 milliseconds, the interval at which BFD packets are received is 10 milliseconds, the local detection time multiplier is 3.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'min-tx-interval min-tx-interval', 'Info': 'Specifies the interval at which BFD packets are sent.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 3 to 20000, in milliseconds. The default value is 10.'}
{'Parameters': 'min-rx-interval min-rx-interval', 'Info': 'Specifies the interval at which BFD packets are received.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 3 to 20000, in milliseconds. The default value is 10.'}
{'Parameters': 'detect-multiplier multiplier', 'Info': 'Specifies the local detection time multiplier.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 3 to 50.'}
