The undo peer connect-interface command restores the default setting.
By default, the outbound interface of a BGP packet serves as the source interface of a BGP packet.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nThe value is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'interface-name', 'Info': 'Specifies an interface name.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 63 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported.'}
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-source-address', 'Info': 'Specifies an IPv4 source address used for establishing a connection.\nThe value is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'interface-type', 'Info': 'Specifies an interface type and number.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'interface-number', 'Info': 'Specifies an interface type and number.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 63 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported.'}
