## User question:
How to configure a Huawei router to use graceful restart mode when resetting BGP connections for all peers in the group named "bgp_peers_group"?
---
## Proposed answer:
graceful-restart peer-reset group bgp_peers_group
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> graceful-restart peer-reset
undo peer <group-name> graceful-restart peer-reset
FuncDef:
The peer graceful-restart peer-reset command enables a device to use the GR mode to reset BGP connections with all peers in a specified group.
The undo peer graceful-restart peer-reset command cancels the enabling configuration.
By default, a device cannot use the GR mode to reset a BGP connection with any peer in a specified group.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a BGP peer group.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters. If spaces are used, the string must start and end with double quotation marks (").'}
