## User question:
How to check the BGP MVPN routes advertised to peer 172.16.25.40 with type 5 (Source Active A-D routes) on a Huawei router?
---
## Proposed answer:
dis bgp vpnv4 all peer 172.16.25.40 route-type 5
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
display bgp mvpn { all | route-distinguisher <route-distinguisher> } routing-table type { 1 | 2 | 3 | 5 | 6 | 7 } <network>
display bgp mvpn vpn-instance <vpn-instance-name> routing-table type { 1 | 2 | 3 | 5 | 6 | 7 } <network>
display bgp mvpn all routing-table peer <ipv4-address> advertised-routes type { 1 | 2 | 3 | 5 | 6 | 7 } <network>
FuncDef:
The display bgp mvpn routing-table type command displays BGP Multicast Virtual Private Network (MVPN) Leaf A-D routes.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'all', 'Info': 'Displays all BGP MVPN routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'route-distinguisher route-distinguisher', 'Info': 'Displays BGP routes of the specified Route Distinguisher (RD).\nThe RD formats are divided into the following types:\n2-byte AS number:4-byte user-defined number, for example, 101:3. An AS number ranges from 0 to 65535. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 4294967295. The AS number and the user-defined number cannot be 0s at the same time. That is, an RD cannot be 0:0.Integral 4-byte AS number:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 65537:3. An AS number ranges from 65536 to 4294967295. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535. The AS number and user-defined number cannot be both 0s. That is, an RD cannot be 0:0.4-byte AS number in dotted notation:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 0.0:3 or 0.1:0.4-byte AS number in dotted notation is in the format of x.y, where x and y are integers that range from 0 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535. The AS number and user-defined number cannot be both 0s. That is, an RD cannot be 0.0:0.IPv4-address:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 192.168.122.15:1. An IP address ranges from 0.0.0.0 to 255.255.255.255. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535.'}
{'Parameters': '1', 'Info': 'Displays intra-AS I-PMSI A-D routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': '2', 'Info': 'Displays S-PMSI A-D routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': '3', 'Info': 'Displays inter-AS I-PMSI A-D routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': '5', 'Info': 'Displays Source Active A-D routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': '6', 'Info': 'Displays Shared Tree Join C-multicast routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': '7', 'Info': 'Displays Source Tree Join C-multicast routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'network', 'Info': 'The meanings of different A-D routes are as follows:\nType 1:Displays an intra-AS I-PMSI A-D route.Type 2:Displays an inter-AS I-PMSI A-D route.Type 3:Displays an S-PMSI A-D route.Type 4:Displays a Leaf A-D route.Type 5:Displays a Source Active A-D route.Type 6:Displays a C-multicast route.Type 7:Displays a C-multicast route.\nDifferent A-D routes have different values:\nType 1:The value is the IP address of the source device, in dotted decimal notation.Type 2:The value is the source AS number. The value is an integer ranging from 1 to 4294967295.Type 3:The value is in the format of X:X::X:X-Y:Y::Y:Y-Z.Z.Z.Z.X:X::X:X represents the multicast source address in an (S, G) entry, in hexadecimal.\nY:Y::Y:Y represents the multicast group address in an (S, G) entry, in hexadecimal.\nZ.Z.Z.Z represents the IP address of the source device, in dotted decimal notation.\nType 4:For the value, see the display bgp mvpn routing-table type 4 route-key-type command.Type 5:The value is in the format of X:X::X:X-Y:Y::Y:Y.X:X::X:X represents the multicast source address in an (S, G) entry, in hexadecimal.\nY:Y::Y:Y represents the multicast group address in an (S, G) entry, in hexadecimal.\nType 6 and Type 7:The value is in the format of AS number:X:X::X:X-Y:Y::Y:Y.AS number: The value is an integer ranging from 1 to 4294967295.\nX:X::X:X represents the multicast source address in an (S, G) entry, in hexadecimal.\nY:Y::Y:Y represents the multicast group address in an (S, G) entry, in hexadecimal.'}
{'Parameters': 'vpn-instance vpn-instance-name', 'Info': 'Displays the BGP routes of the specified VPN instance.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 31 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported. In addition, the VPN instance name must not be _public_. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'peer ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Displays the routes of the specified BGP peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'advertised-routes', 'Info': 'Displays the routes advertised to the specified peer.\n-'}
