## User question:
Configure the Keepalive interval to 15 seconds and Hold time to 90 seconds for BGP peer 192.168.50.25 on Huawei routers.
---
## Proposed answer:
peer 192.168.50.25 timer keepalive 15 hold 90
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> timer keepalive <keepalive-time> hold <hold-time>
peer <ipv4-address> timer keepalive <keepalive-time> hold <hold-time> min-holdtime <min-hold-value>
undo peer <ipv4-address> timer keepalive hold
undo peer <ipv4-address> timer keepalive <keepalive-time> hold <hold-time>
undo peer <ipv4-address> timer
undo peer <ipv4-address> timer keepalive hold min-holdtime
undo peer <ipv4-address> timer keepalive <keepalive-time> hold <hold-time> min-holdtime <min-hold-value>
FuncDef:
The peer timer command sets the Keepalive time and hold time for a peer.
The undo peer timer command restores the default Keepalive time and hold time.
By default, the Keepalive time is 60s, and the hold time is 180s.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nThe value is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'keepalive keepalive-time', 'Info': 'Specifies the Keepalive time.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 0 to 21845, in seconds. The default value is 60 seconds.'}
{'Parameters': 'hold hold-time', 'Info': 'Indicates the hold time.\nThe value is an integer that can be 0, or ranges from 3 to 65535, in seconds. The default value is 180 seconds.\nSetting the hold time of a BGP peer to be longer than 20s is recommended. If the hold time of a BGP peer is shorter than 20s, the session may be closed.'}
{'Parameters': 'min-holdtime min-hold-value', 'Info': 'Specifies the minimum hold time. On the same device, min-hold-value must be less than hold-time.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 20 to 65535, in seconds.'}
