ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'all', 'Info': 'Displays all BGP IPv6 MVPN routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'route-distinguisher route-distinguisher', 'Info': 'Displays BGP routes of the specified Route Distinguisher (RD).\nThe RD formats are divided into the following types:\n2-byte AS number:4-byte user-defined number, for example, 101:3. An AS number ranges from 0 to 65535. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 4294967295. The AS number and the user-defined number cannot be 0s at the same time. That is, an RD cannot be 0:0.Integral 4-byte AS number:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 65537:3. An AS number ranges from 65536 to 4294967295. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535. The AS number and user-defined number cannot be both 0s. That is, an RD cannot be 0:0.4-byte AS number in dotted notation:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 0.0:3 or 0.1:0.4-byte AS number in dotted notation is in the format of x.y, wherex and y are integers that range from 0 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535. The AS number and user-defined number cannot be both 0s. That is, an RD cannot be 0.0:0.IPv4-address:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 192.168.122.15:1. An IP address ranges from 0.0.0.0 to 255.255.255.255. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535.'}
{'Parameters': '1', 'Info': 'Displays intra-AS I-PMSI A-D routes.\n-'}
