## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
router-id <ipv4-address>
undo router-id
FuncDef:
The router-id command configures a Router ID for the Router. Each Router ID uniquely identifies one Router in an AS.
The undo router-id command deletes the Router ID configured for the Router.
By default, no BGP Router ID is configured, and the Router ID configured for the route management module through the router id command is used.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
