## User question:
Set the global BGP ConnectRetry interval to 45 seconds on a Huawei router.
---
## Proposed answer:
bgp 100 connect-retry 45
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
timer connect-retry <connect-retry-time>
undo timer connect-retry
FuncDef:
The timer connect-retry command sets a global ConnectRetry interval.
The undo timer connect-retry command restores the default setting.
By default, the ConnectRetry interval is 32s.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'connect-retry-time', 'Info': 'Specifies a ConnectRetry interval.\nThe value ranges from 1 to 65535, in seconds.'}
