## User question:
In Huawei router's BGP multi-instance configuration, how to set the keepalive time to 40 seconds and hold time to 120 seconds with a minimum hold time of 80 seconds?
---
## Proposed answer:
commit
bgp 100 instance p1
peer 10.1.1.1 timer keepalive 40 hold 120 min-holdtime 80
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
timer keepalive <keepalive-time> hold <hold-time> [ min-holdtime <min-hold-value> ]
undo timer keepalive hold [ min-holdtime ]
undo timer keepalive <keepalive-time> hold <hold-time> [ min-holdtime <min-hold-value> ]
FuncDef:
The timer keepalive hold command sets the Keepalive time and hold time.
The undo timer keepalive hold command restores the default Keepalive time and hold time.
By default, the Keepalive time is 60s, and the hold time is 180s.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'hold hold-time', 'Info': 'Specifies the hold time.\nThe value is an integer that can be 0, or ranges from 3 to 65535, in seconds.'}
{'Parameters': 'min-holdtime min-hold-value', 'Info': 'Specifies the minimum hold time. On the same device, min-hold-value must be less than hold-time.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 20 to 65535, in seconds.'}
{'Parameters': 'keepalive keepalive-time', 'Info': 'Specifies the Keepalive time.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 0 to 21845, in seconds.'}
