## User question:
How to configure Huawei router's BGP multi-instance VPN to import OSPF process 45 routes with MED value 500 and apply route-policy "POLICY_OSPF"?
---
## Proposed answer:
ip vpn-instance vpna
ipv6-family
route-distinguisher 100:1
vpn-target 111:1 both
quit
bgp 100 instance a
ipv6-family vpn-instance vpna
import-route ospf 45 med 500 route-policy POLICY_OSPF
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
import-route { static | direct | unr | op-route } [ [ med <med-value> ] | [ [ route-policy <route-policy-name> ] | [ route-filter <route-filter-name> ] ] ] *
import-route { unr | { ospf | isis | rip } <processId> } [ [ med <med-value> ] | [ [ route-policy <route-policy-name> ] | [ route-filter <route-filter-name> ] ] ] *
undo import-route { static | direct | unr | op-route }
undo import-route { { ospf | isis | rip } <processId> }
FuncDef:
The import-route command configures BGP to import routes from other protocols.
The undo import-route command cancels the configuration.
By default, BGP does not import routes from other protocols.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'static', 'Info': 'Configures BGP to import static routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'direct', 'Info': 'Configures BGP to import direct routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'unr', 'Info': 'Configures BGP to import UNR routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'op-route', 'Info': 'Configures BGP to import open programming (OP)-routes.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'med med-value', 'Info': 'Specifies the MED for imported routes.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 0 to 4294967295.'}
{'Parameters': 'route-policy route-policy-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the route-policy used to filter routes and modify route attributes when these routes are imported from other protocols.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 200 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'route-filter route-filter-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the route-filter used to filter routes and modify route attributes when these routes are imported from other protocols.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 200 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported. If parameters are included in the referenced route-filter, specify values for them in the format of (var1, var2, ...var8) behind the route-filter name. A maximum of eight parameters can be specified, and each value ranges from 1 to 200 characters.'}
