## User question:
How to configure a Huawei router to advertise BGP community attributes to peer 192.168.50.25 in a multi-instance VPNv4 environment?
---
## Proposed answer:
ip vpn-instance vpna
ipv4-family
route-distinguisher 100:1
vpn-target 111:1 both
quit
bgp 100 instance a
ipv4-family vpn-instance vrf1
peer 192.168.50.25 as-number 100
peer 192.168.50.25 advertise-community
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> advertise-community
undo peer <ipv4-address> advertise-community
FuncDef:
The peer advertise-community command configures a device to advertise a community attribute to its peer.
The undo peer advertise-community command cancels the existing configuration.
By default, a device advertises no community attribute to its peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
