## User question:
How to configure Huawei router to filter BGP VPNv4 routes advertised to peer 192.168.50.25 using basic ACL 2100?
---
## Proposed answer:
acl 2100
rule permit
quit
bgp 100
peer 192.168.50.25 as-number 100
ipv4-family vpnv4
peer 192.168.50.25 enable
peer 192.168.50.25 filter-policy 2100 export
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> filter-policy <acl-number> export
peer <ipv4-address> filter-policy acl-name <acl-name> export
undo peer <ipv4-address> filter-policy <acl-number> export
undo peer <ipv4-address> filter-policy acl-name <acl-name> export
FuncDef:
The peer filter-policy export command configures an ACL-based policy for filtering BGP routes to be advertised to a specified peer.
The undo peer filter-policy export command cancels this configuration.
By default, no filtering policy is set for a peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'acl-number', 'Info': 'Specifies the number of a basic ACL.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 2000 to 2999.'}
{'Parameters': 'export', 'Info': 'Filters routes to be advertised.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'acl-name acl-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a named basic ACL.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 64 case-sensitive characters without spaces. The value must start with a letter (a to z or A to Z, case sensitive).'}
