The display bgp l2vpn-ad routing-table vpws command displays statistics about VPWS routes in the BGP L2VPN-AD routing table.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'route-distinguisher route-distinguisher', 'Info': 'Specifies a route distinguisher.\nThe RD formats are divided into the following types:\n2-byte AS number:4-byte user-defined number, for example, 101:3. An AS number ranges from 0 to 65535. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 4294967295. The AS number and the user-defined number cannot be 0s at the same time. That is, an RD cannot be 0:0.Integral 4-byte AS number:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 65537:3. An AS number ranges from 65536 to 4294967295. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535. The AS number and user-defined number cannot be both 0s. That is, an RD cannot be 0:0.4-byte AS number in dotted notation:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 0.0:3 or 0.1:0.4-byte AS number in dotted notation is in the format of x.y, wherex and y are integers that range from 0 to 65535 and from 0 to 65535, respectively. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535. The AS number and user-defined number cannot be both 0s. That is, an RD cannot be 0.0:0.IPv4-address:2-byte user-defined number, for example, 192.168.122.15:1. An IP address ranges from 0.0.0.0 to 255.255.255.255. A user-defined number ranges from 0 to 65535.'}
{'Parameters': 'ce-id ce-id', 'Info': 'Displays statistics about VPWS routes with the specified CE ID.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 0 to 65535.'}
{'Parameters': 'label-offset label-offset', 'Info': 'Displays statistics about VPWS routes with the specified label offset.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 0 to 65535.'}
{'Parameters': 'peer ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Displays information about BFD sessions of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'advertised-routes', 'Info': 'Displays statistics about VPWS routes advertised to the specified peer.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'received-routes', 'Info': 'Displays statistics about VPWS routes received from the specified peer.\n-'}
