## User question:
How to configure Huawei router to filter BGP routes advertised to peer 192.168.50.30 using IP prefix list named "custA-routes"?
---
## Proposed answer:
ip ip-prefix custA-routes index 10 permit 192.168.50.0 24
bgp 100
peer 192.168.50.30 as-number 200
ipv4-family vpnv4
peer 192.168.50.30 enable
peer 192.168.50.30 ip-prefix custA-routes export
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> ip-prefix <ip-prefix-name> export
undo peer <ipv4-address> ip-prefix [ <ip-prefix-name> ] export
FuncDef:
The peer ip-prefix export command configures a policy based on an IP prefix list for filtering BGP routes to be advertised to a specified peer.
The undo peer ip-prefix export command cancels this configuration.
By default, no route filtering policy based on an IP address prefix list is configured for a peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'ip-prefix ip-prefix-name', 'Info': 'specifies the name of an IP address prefix list.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 169 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'export', 'Info': 'Applies a filtering policy to the routes to be advertised to a peer.\n-'}
---
