## User question:
How to configure Huawei router to filter incoming BGP VPNv4 routes from peer 192.168.50.20 using IP prefix list named "custA_filter"?
---
## Proposed answer:
ip ip-prefix custA_filter permit 10.1.1.0 24
bgp 100
peer 192.168.50.20 as-number 100
ipv4-family vpnv4
peer 192.168.50.20 enable
peer 192.168.50.20 ip-prefix custA_filter import
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> ip-prefix <ip-prefix-name> import
undo peer <ipv4-address> ip-prefix [ <ip-prefix-name> ] import
FuncDef:
The peer ip-prefix import command configures a policy based on an IP prefix list for filtering BGP routes received from a specified peer.
The undo peer ip-prefix import command cancels this configuration.
By default, no route filtering policy based on an IP address prefix list is configured for a peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'ip-prefix ip-prefix-name', 'Info': 'specifies the name of an IP address prefix list.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 169 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'import', 'Info': 'Applies a filtering policy to the routes received from a peer.\n-'}
