## User question:
Configure intervals on Huawei routers for BGP recursion suppression when next hop flapping occurs: increase penalty after 40 seconds, retain penalty for 90 seconds, and clear penalty after 300 seconds.
---
## Proposed answer:
nexthop recursive-lookup restrain suppress-interval 40 hold-interval 90 clear-interval 300
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
nexthop recursive-lookup restrain suppress-interval <add-count-time> hold-interval <hold-count-time> clear-interval <clear-count-time>
undo nexthop recursive-lookup restrain suppress-interval hold-interval clear-interval
FuncDef:
The nexthop recursive-lookup restrain command configures the intervals for increasing, retaining, and clearing the penalty value for BGP recursion suppression in case of next hop flapping.
The undo nexthop recursive-lookup restrain command restores the default configuration.
By default, the intervals for increasing, retaining, and clearing the penalty value for BGP recursion suppression in case of next hop flapping are 60s, 120s, and 600s, respectively.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'hold-interval hold-count-time', 'Info': 'Specifies the interval for retaining the penalty value for recursion suppression.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 65535, in seconds. The default values is recommended.'}
{'Parameters': 'clear-interval clear-count-time', 'Info': 'Specifies the interval for clearing the penalty value for recursion suppression.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 65535, in seconds. The default values is recommended.'}
{'Parameters': 'suppress-interval add-count-time', 'Info': 'Specifies the interval for increasing the penalty value for recursion suppression.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 65535, in seconds. The default value is recommended.'}
---
